cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research code, please cite the repository."
title: "S&P 500 Variance Risk Premium and Synthetic Gamma Scalping"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shah
    given-names: Bhavya
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bhavya-project1/spx-variance-risk-premium-research"
abstract: >-
  Empirical research comparing HAR, GARCH(1,1), and GJR-GARCH(1,1)
  forecasts for S&P 500 realised variance and a VIX-based variance risk
  premium proxy. The notebook includes out-of-sample forecast evaluation,
  statistical robustness procedures, and a synthetic Black-Scholes
  delta-hedged straddle and E-mini futures hedging simulation. Synthetic
  option results are modelling experiments and are not historical
  executable-options performance.
keywords:
  - quantitative finance
  - variance risk premium
  - volatility forecasting
  - HAR
  - GARCH
  - GJR-GARCH
  - options
  - delta hedging
  - gamma scalping
  - S&P 500
